\subsection{The harm is absorbed by the floor}

One more experiment closes the $2\times2$'s logic. Run the exact-prior arm with symbolic structure attached and the harm disappears: at the exact tier, the gated variant lands within $0.0001$\,px of the ungated one (paired ratio $0.0005$), while the gate's occupancy pathology is unchanged---the same handful of experts alive, the same dead classes (2--15 of 64 occupied depending on the variant; Table~\ref{tab:c3}). The structure still wastes capacity; the waste no longer costs anything, because the residual head has nothing to be wrong about. This is why the subtraction result and the floor result are one result: the harm of structure is a tax on the residual signal, and the residual signal is bounded by the floor.

