\section{Negative-result catalogue}\label{app:negative}
Table~\ref{tab:c3} gives the full accounting behind C3---the four
experiment generations, the pairing each comparison actually uses, and
the routing audit.
\input{tab_c3_gating}

The paper's claims are paired with the following preregistered negative results, reported at the same standard as the positive ones. Structure and supervision: symbolic gating (four experiment generations, 7/7 paired variants negative); label supervision (2$\times$2, 6/6 negative); end-to-end gating (gradient starvation); supervised gating (co-adaptation). Loss geometry and identification: loss-mass dose (ceiling and reversal); indicator training (no ROC shift); single-step identification of parameters (compensation basin). Two further negatives are reported without a figure or table: confidence-gated source switching (no benefit) and multi-hypothesis prediction in a deterministic world (mode collapse). Table~\ref{tab:criteria} in Appendix~\ref{app:criteria} lists the criteria and their outcomes slot by slot, including the thresholds that missed; an English summary of every criterion accompanies the paper as \texttt{PREREG\_CRITERIA\_EN.md}, and crash accounting is in the preregistration files.

\paragraph{One pair of readings we report against ourselves.} The identification slot was first scored by an earlier criterion set that asked the clean-world estimate to land within $\pm20\%$ of the true value; it misses ($705.7$ against $900$, $21.6\%$ low), and the two companion criteria for the perturbed world (rollout recovery, and the parameter within $\pm20\%$ of $1125$) miss as well---three of six criteria, in all three seeds. The preregistration of \S\ref{sec:floor} supersedes that set by scoring the same basin as a replication target rather than as truth recovery, and it passes $3/3$; we report both readings rather than the passing one. Per-seed verdicts for both sets are in the S2 identification reports.




